      <h3>1.2 Anatomy of a Webpage — The DOM</h3>
      <p>When a browser loads an HTML file, it doesn't just display it as-is. It parses the HTML and constructs a
        <strong>Document Object Model (DOM)</strong> — a tree-like representation of all the elements on the page and
        their relationships.</p>
      <p>Think of the DOM like a family tree. The <code>&lt;html&gt;</code> element is the great-grandparent. Inside it,
        <code>&lt;head&gt;</code> and <code>&lt;body&gt;</code> are the children. Inside <code>&lt;body&gt;</code> are
        paragraphs, images, and other elements — grandchildren and great-grandchildren. Every element knows its parent,
        siblings, and descendants.</p>

