      <h3>1.8 Responsive Design — One Structure, All Screens</h3>
      <p>Modern websites must work on phones, tablets, laptops, and TVs. <strong>Responsive design</strong> is the
        approach of building a single site that intelligently adapts its layout to fit any screen size using <em>CSS
          media queries</em>, flexible grids, and fluid images.</p>
      <p>Example: A desktop layout might show 3 columns of articles side by side. On a tablet, they collapse to 2
        columns. On a phone, each article takes the full width, stacked vertically.</p>
      <div class="callout callout-tip">
        <strong>Key metric:</strong> As of 2024, over 60% of all web traffic comes from mobile devices. A non-responsive
        website is essentially broken for the majority of modern users.
      </div>
    </section>

